EXPERIMENT 15 – CAPTURING SCREENSHOT USING SELENIUM

AIM
To write a Selenium WebDriver program to capture a screenshot of a web page and store it in the local system.
ALGORITHM
1. Create a Maven project and add the Selenium 4 dependency.
2. Open the web page using driver.get().
3. Use TakesScreenshot and getScreenshotAs() to capture the screenshot.
4. Create a folder named screenshots.
5. Copy the temporary screenshot as home_page.png using Files.copy().
6. Print the saved file path.
CODE
Exercise15.java
import org.openqa.selenium.*;
import org.openqa.selenium.chrome.ChromeDriver;
import java.io.File;
import java.nio.file.Files;
import java.nio.file.Path;
import java.nio.file.Paths;
import java.nio.file.StandardCopyOption;

public class Exercise15 {
    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        WebDriver driver = new ChromeDriver();

        try {
            driver.manage().window().maximize();

            driver.get("https://the-internet.herokuapp.com");

            File source = ((TakesScreenshot) driver)
                .getScreenshotAs(OutputType.FILE);

            Path dest = Paths.get(
                "screenshots", "home_page.png"
            );

            Files.createDirectories(dest.getParent());

            Files.copy(
                source.toPath(),
                dest,
                StandardCopyOption.REPLACE_EXISTING
            );

            System.out.println(
                "Screenshot saved at : " + dest.toAbsolutePath()
            );

        } finally {
            driver.quit();
        }
    }
}


INPUT
- Website: https://the-internet.herokuapp.com
- Screenshot filename: home_page.png
- Folder name: screenshots
OUTPUT
Screenshot saved at :
<project-folder>/screenshots/home_page.png


RESULT
Thus, the Selenium WebDriver program to capture a screenshot of a web page and store it in the local system was executed successfully.
